1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,580
 So I'm on the AWS console.

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:04,680
 Let me just search for translate.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,840
 And here we have Amazon translate.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:12,000
 And it says Amazon translate provides fast, affordable,

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,720
 and quality translation for your multi-lingual needs.

6
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,560
 So you can do a launch real-time translation.

7
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:22,000
 And here you can see two options.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
 So you have batch translation.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,240
 And if I just click on this create job,

10
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,720
 and I just give the name of a job.

11
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,360
 And then I select source language.

12
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:34,120
 So what is the language for my source text?

13
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,240
 And I can select one of them, or I can also select auto.

14
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,640
 And it will auto detect.

15
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,240
 And then then I have the target language in which language

16
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:45,960
 I want this text to be translated to.

17
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:51,000
 And then I can upload my document in S3 bucket.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,200
 And I have to give the location of S3 bucket

19
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,920
 and just give the format.

20
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:58,280
 Whether it's HTML, Word, Document, Excel, and so on.

21
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,320
 Then I also need to provide the location of S3 bucket

22
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:04,840
 where the output data after the Amazon translate

23
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:08,240
 has translated would be stored in.

24
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,440
 And then you have customization options.

25
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,560
 You can click on formality.

26
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:15,680
 Whether you want the translation to be formal, informal.

27
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:20,120
 You can also do profanity masking if you make like.

28
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:24,160
 And then if I just go back to Amazon translate and click here.

29
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:26,640
 And then if I do real-time translation,

30
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:28,600
 it can be the text or document.

31
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,320
 So source language, you can do auto detection,

32
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:36,160
 or you can select one of the languages from the 75 languages.

33
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:39,440
 Then you can select the target language here.

34
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:42,600
 Let me just select the target language as maybe German.

35
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:47,600
 And let me enter the text here.

36
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:53,160
 We say-- and let me just say, welcome to my Udemy course.

37
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,800
 And you can see it's translated in German.

38
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,200
 So I'm not conversant with German.

39
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,920
 So hopefully it is translated correctly.

40
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,120
 And then you can choose some additional settings

41
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:12,280
 like custom terminology, brevity, formality, profanity masking,

42
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,560
 and so on.

43
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:17,520
 So that's at a high level how Amazon translate works.

44
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,720
 So hopefully we have gotten high level overview

45
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,200
 of how Amazon translate works.

46
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,240
 I'll see you in the next lecture.

47
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,800
 Thank you.

